      "mergeID": "6352ec8c06fe04732aacc938",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Situations where I or a friends are already in a private world and have access to the \"World Details\" panel.\nI can create a new instance using the \"New Instance\" button.\nPreviously it was grayed out in private worlds.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1238] Can create new instance of other's private world from menu.",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "634b5912eb602b451d40008a",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 1
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Similar post with Live version now. \nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/access-to-private-worlds\nI'm quoting what I commented over there\n-\nIf the WorldID is known, Instance can be created from the Web or API even in private worlds. \nBut I'd like to ask for an explanation that with this update why \"New Instance\" button that were not available before can now be used.\nI'd like to confirm whether if this change was intended.\nIf it's a spec, then I don't mind.\n-",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
