      "value": "@{5b7fb61894211b58b866e8ae|full_name}: \"aren't a bug anyway if you have to get to them through manipulating strings\"\n\nThat sounds nonsensical. Of course it is a bug if you are able to do something you weren't supposed to be able to do. It should be easy for the website/client to check if the instance being created/joined is public and the world is private and then give an error message. But as I mentioned in the bug report itself, it is a very minor issue and not all that important since they aren't truly public anyway.\n\nBut as mentioned in my comment before, I would love to see multiple levels of world privacy. It would make a lot more sense to have a difference between \"private worlds\" and \"unlisted worlds\". Should I make a separate feature request for that? (Assuming a feature request doesn't already exist.)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
